.TH "ROARK\-CONNECTIONS\-AGENT\-UPDATE" "1" "" "roark-connections-agent-update" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-connections\-agent\-update \- Update an agent connection
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark connections agent update
\fIconnection\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Changes a connection’s settings or rotates its credential. Send `provider` (it must match the connection’s) and only the fields to change; the rest keep their stored values. A new Retell, Vapi, ElevenLabs or Bland key is checked by listing agents first. Moving to `agentScope` ALL, or giving an ALL connection a new key, on an account with more agents than the project allows returns 400 `too_many_agents`, as does selecting more than 1,000. Set `status` to INACTIVE to pause syncing without deleting anything.
.SH "API"
PATCH /v1/connections/agent/{connectionId}
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIconnection\-id\fR
The connection\-id.
.SH "REQUEST BODY"
This endpoint accepts one of several request shapes, so the body is supplied as JSON through \e\-\e\-data or on standard input rather than as individual flags.
